{
  "summary": "The report documents a 47-minute payment processing outage on August 12, 2024 (14:23–15:10 UTC), caused by database migration lock contention, which affected the Payment API, Refunds API, and Webhooks. The incident breached the uptime SLAs of three contracts: MSA-2023-001 (Acme Corp, 99.9%), MSA-2023-007 (Global Industries, 99.95%), and MSA-2023-012 (TechStart Ventures, 99.9%). August downtime to date reached 52 minutes, exceeding each contract's allowed downtime budget and resulting in SLA breaches for all three clients. Service credits total $6,250: $1,000 for Acme Corp (10% of a $10,000 monthly fee), $3,750 for Global Industries (15% of a $25,000 monthly fee), and $1,500 for TechStart (10% of a $15,000 monthly fee). All three clients were notified during the incident and acknowledged the notifications. Remediation includes deploying connection pool monitoring by August 15, adding migration safety gates in CI/CD by August 30, and evaluating online schema change tools by September 30. Contractual next steps are to issue service credit invoices by August 20, schedule SLA review meetings with each client by August 25, and update runbooks and incident response procedures by September 15."
}
